 "uncertain": [
  "drivers.M0.silkscreen.STEP 'PE11': the lower stroke of the 'E' is hidden under a cyan dashed overlay line, so E vs F cannot be fully confirmed from the silkscreen alone. The X-MOT inset clearly shows PE11.",
  "drivers.M1.inset.DIAG19 'Y-:PB13': the hyphen after 'Y' sits on the dashed leader line, so 'Y-:' vs 'Y:' is slightly ambiguous at 5x zoom. The MCU pin PB13 itself is clear.",
  "exp2 callout prints 'BP10' (confirmed at 5x); board silkscreen for EXP2 and SD CD both print 'PB10'. Recorded verbatim. Treating it as PB10 is an inference from the silkscreen.",
  "pi_uart top row: the callout shows NC,NC,NC,NC,GND, but the board silkscreen shows NC,SDA,SCL,NC,GND. The sheet contradicts itself on whether positions 2-3 carry SDA/SCL.",
  "can: the callout pairs 'L' with PD0 and 'H' with PD1. These are MCU pin names under bus-line letters. The sheet does not say which is CAN RX or TX. PD0/PD1 are also printed on EXP1.",
  "fans silkscreen (FAN0 PA13, FAN1 PA14, FAN2 PB2, FAN3-5) and endstop silkscreen row: lower parts of glyphs are overlapped by dashed overlay lines. They are legible and match the clean callouts, so the values are taken from the callouts.",
  "No MCU pin is printed anywhere for: Pi UART RX/TX, I2C SDA/SCL, probe SIG / Z- / IO / CLK / BT0, SD RST, or the VCC/B/R/G header. These are left as 'none printed', not guessed.",
  "probe callout 'BTO' (letter O) vs silkscreen 'BT0' (digit 0); USB callout 'UVCC' vs silkscreen 'U5V'. These are naming differences only, not MCU pins.",
  "60Vmax: only the X-MOT and Y-MOT insets say '(60Vmax)'. Nothing on the board render says 60V; the red socket headers on M0/M1 only support this indirectly."
 ],
